#!/bin/bash
# land-metal-and-loose.sh — three metals priced by the gram at the day's rate,
# and the option to just buy the stone.
#
# BOTH SIDES (together-city-chat + together-city-react). Vercel AND Railway.
# AFTER PUSHING, set the rates on Railway (see the notes the script prints).
# PRECONDITION: land-gem-studio.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="A gold price goes stale in a day"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"A gemstone is a commission"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-gem-studio.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="71fa5c016e814b2b206b0e8e8b679afbc53fedf68e7edd7824c41ef1ed367291"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

echo "== gates: the API"
cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/astrology
cd ..

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/src/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/app/one-stone-answer.test.ts
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
A gold price goes stale in a day

THREE METALS, PRICED BY THE GRAM. 22 carat gold, silver, and panchdhatu — the
traditional alloy, which the wearing table already names for several of the
planets, so it is the honest third option rather than a generic "metal". The one
the tradition names for THIS stone's planet is marked; the other two are still
there, because silver instead of gold is a legitimate choice and often the one
somebody can actually make.

THE WEIGHT IS ESTIMATED FROM THREE REAL THINGS and the file says they are
estimates: the mount (a cluster carries far more gold than a solitaire), the
size (a size 22 band is meaningfully more metal than a size 8), and the stone (a
big gem needs a bigger seat). So the quote is asked for again whenever the mount
or the size changes — a single number on the page would have been wrong for
almost everybody.

That is also why it is its own endpoint. The first attempt handed the design
payload a FUNCTION to call for a quote, which does not survive JSON and would
have arrived as nothing at all.

THE RATE IS READ FROM THE ENVIRONMENT. Twenty-two carat gold moved by a fifth
across 2025 alone, and a rate compiled into a deployed file is a shop quoting
last quarter with total confidence. GOLD_22K_INR_PER_G, SILVER_INR_PER_G and
PANCHDHATU_INR_PER_G override the dated fallbacks, so a correction takes a
minute and no deploy, and METAL_RATES_AS_OF travels with them so the staleness
is visible to us rather than only to the citizen's bank. The fallbacks are
indicative, like the gem prices in the data sheet, and this file is where a
live feed lands.

THE MAKING CHARGE IS FIFTEEN PER CENT, INSIDE THE QUOTED PRICE, and never shown
as a line — the owner's instruction, and ordinary jewellery retail practice: the
price shown is the price paid and nothing is added at checkout. It is documented
in metal-pricing.ts and asserted in its spec specifically so that nobody later
"fixes" the quote by adding a making charge on top of one that already contains
it. That mistake is invisible in the code and obvious on the invoice.

Nothing about the price is computed in the browser. The rate, the weight model
and the making charge live in one server file, and the commission endpoint
prices the stone and the metal again from that same file rather than trusting
the page's sum.

AND YOU CAN JUST BUY THE STONE. A third route beside ring and pendant: loose and
unset, for a jeweller somebody already trusts or a setting in the family that
wants a new stone in it. Refusing to sell them the gem would hold the thing they
came for hostage to a service they did not ask for.

It still leaves with the specification — set in this metal, on this finger, of
this hand, with an OPEN BACK, first worn on this day — because an unset stone
and no instructions is half a purchase, and the open back is the part jewellers
most often close up and the whole point of a prescribed stone. It goes on the
receipt so it can be handed over as it is. No metal is charged for and the page
says why: setting it is between them and their jeweller.
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: A gold price goes stale in a day

 SET THESE ON RAILWAY before anybody buys gold — the fallbacks
 are indicative figures dated 1 Aug 2026, not a live rate:

   GOLD_22K_INR_PER_G     e.g. 9000
   SILVER_INR_PER_G       e.g. 110
   PANCHDHATU_INR_PER_G   e.g. 900
   METAL_RATES_AS_OF      e.g. 2026-08-11

 Then push. Vercel rebuilds the web app; Railway redeploys the
 API and picks the rates up.
===============================================================

DONE
